    schema1:audience "neuroimaging researchers" ;
    schema1:codeRepository <https://github.com/incf-nidash/PyNIDM> ;
    schema1:description "Python library and CLI for the Neuroimaging Data Model: bidsmri2nidm converts a BIDS dataset to NIDM, csv2nidm annotates tabular phenotype data with terms, and pynidm query runs SPARQL over NIDM files; it also has linear-regression and merge tools. Use it to build or query NIDM graphs from BIDS plus spreadsheets. Its in-memory query is slow on many files (the simple2 README warns it is too long beyond ~10 files)." ;
